
                                            26 OCT 2025


FROM: Leidos, Inc 
      3203 General Hudnell Suite 301
      San Antonio TX, 78266

SUBJECT: AFTER ACTION REPORT

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
   
   • Mission: Provide technical support to 902nd CPT at Vandenberg Listening Station, CA
   • Problem: Intermittent sensor failures requiring periodic restart/redeployment of CVAH systems
   • Duration: 23-28 October 2025 (6 days)
   • Outcome: Root cause identified and remediation procedures established

2. DAILY ACTIVITIES

   Day 1 (23 OCT): Initial coordination and travel to Santa Maria, CA. Met with SSgt Johnson and George Arechega.

   Day 2 (24 OCT): System evaluation revealed no active faults. Identified PID 741873 memory spikes and cronQueries configuration warnings in Arkime container logs.

   Day 3 (25 OCT): Modified Elastic Watcher configuration to reduce excessive logging and improve efficiency. Identified potential need for Arkime reinstallation.

   Day 4 (26 OCT): Continued monitoring showed stable packet capture. Watcher modifications required re-application. Scheduled automated snapshots for low-traffic periods.

   Day 5 (27 OCT): Sensor 2 developed similar issues. Redeployed Sensor 5 with enhanced specifications (40GB RAM, 500K message queue). Reinstalled Arkime on Sensor 2 with 64GB RAM.

   Day 6 (28 OCT): Implemented optimized Arkime configurations on multiple sensors with lighter, faster processing settings.

3. ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS

   • Primary Issue: Arkime memory saturation during high network traffic periods
   • Contributing Factors:
     - Default configuration insufficient for traffic volume
     - Disk I/O unable to keep pace with packet ingestion
     - Oversized bulk operations causing memory locks
     - Network intermittency creating incomplete packet captures

4. LESSONS LEARNED

   • Maintain backup lightweight sensors with tap capability for failover
   • Avoid modifying Kubernetes pods/containers (changes not persistent)
   • Network intermittency can cause Elasticsearch index recovery loops
   • Default Arkime configurations inadequate for high-traffic environments

5. RECOMMENDATIONS

   Implement the following Arkime configuration modifications for high-traffic deployments:

   Configuration Parameters:
   ┌─────────────────────┬──────────────┬────────────┐
   │ Parameter           │ Value        │ Action     │
   ├─────────────────────┼──────────────┼────────────┤
   │ mem_limit           │ 24Gi         │ Modify     │
   │ cpu_request         │ 3000         │ Modify     │
   │ maxFileSizeG        │ 25           │ Modify     │
   │ freespaceG          │ 15%          │ Modify     │
   │ spiDataMaxIndices   │ 15           │ Modify     │
   │ packetThreads       │ 6            │ Modify     │
   │ pcapWriteMethod     │ simple       │ Modify     │
   │ pcapWriteSize       │ 1048576      │ Modify     │
   │ dbBulkSize          │ 150000       │ Modify     │
   │ maxESConns          │ 30           │ Modify     │
   │ maxESRequests       │ 200          │ Modify     │
   │ packetsPerPoll      │ 500000       │ Modify     │
   │ magicMode           │ basic        │ Modify     │
   │ tpacketv3BlockSize  │ 8388608      │ Modify     │
   │ tpacketv3NumThreads │ 4            │ Modify     │
   │ maxPacketsInQueue   │ 150000       │ Modify     │
   │ rotateIndex         │ hourly4      │ Modify     │
   │ maxstreams          │ 200000       │ Add        │
   │ maxPackets          │ 3000         │ Add        │
   │ compressES          │ true         │ Add        │
   └─────────────────────┴──────────────┴────────────┘

   Note: Apply these settings during Arkime reinstallation via CVAH configuration interface.

